 "Navigate independently to the official service and follow incident procedures.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 6}, {"id": "cloud-07", "category": "cloud", "category_name": "Cloud & Productivity", "difficulty": "Advanced", "type": "scenario", "title": "A team needs to collaborate on one document. What is usually preferable", "prompt": "A team needs to collaborate on one document. What is usually preferable?", "options": ["Use approved shared document with least-privilege access", "Email many conflicting copies", "Share one account password", "Make it public to everyone"], "explanation": "A shared controlled document avoids version confusion and excess access.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 7}, {"id": "cloud-08", "category": "cloud", "category_name": "Cloud & Productivity", "difficulty": "Advanced", "type": "identify-the-error", "title": "A mailbox is full. What should support review", "prompt": "A mailbox is full. What should support review?", "options": ["Storage usage, retention and large items under policy", "Delete all mail blindly", "Disable security updates", "Replace keyboard"], "explanation": "Review mailbox quota and retention rules before deleting data.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 8}, {"id": "cloud-09", "category": "cloud", "category_name": "Cloud & Productivity", "difficulty": "Advanced", "type": "multiple-choice", "title": "A user is signed into the wrong cloud account. What should they do", "prompt": "A user is signed into the wrong cloud account. What should they do?", "options": ["Confirm account identity and switch using approved sign-out/sign-in steps", "Share both passwords", "Delete the browser", "Disable account protection"], "explanation": "Correct account context often resolves access and sync confusion.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 9}, {"id": "cloud-10", "category": "cloud", "category_name": "Cloud & Productivity", "difficulty": "Advanced", "type": "scenario", "title": "Why use least-privilege sharing", "prompt": "Why use least-privilege sharing?", "options": ["Give users only the access needed for their task", "Make every file public", "Avoid authentication", "Increase attachment size"], "explanation": "Least privilege reduces accidental exposure and unnecessary access.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 10}, {"id": "infrastructure-01", "category": "infrastructure", "category_name": "Servers & IT Infrastructure", "difficulty": "Beginner", "type": "multiple-choice", "title": "A new employee needs access to a shared folder. What should be confirmed first", "prompt": "A new employee needs access to a shared folder. What should be confirmed first?", "options": ["Approved request and required role-based permissions", "Their personal email password", "Monitor model", "Favourite browser"], "explanation": "Access should follow approval and least-privilege policy.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 1}, {"id": "infrastructure-02", "category": "infrastructure", "category_name": "Servers & IT Infrastructure", "difficulty": "Beginner", "type": "scenario", "title": "A server disk is nearly full. What should an administrator do", "prompt": "A server disk is nearly full. What should an administrator do?", "options": ["Review disk usage, logs and growth before approved cleanup or expansion", "Delete random system files", "Disable monitoring", "Ignore alerts"], "explanation": "Identify what is consuming space and protect system/application data.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 2}, {"id": "infrastructure-03", "category": "infrastructure", "category_name": "Servers & IT Infrastructure", "difficulty": "Beginner", "type": "identify-the-error", "title": "Why are server backups tested", "prompt": "Why are server backups tested?", "options": ["To verify data can actually be restored", "To increase CPU speed", "To change DNS names", "To remove access controls"], "explanation": "A backup is useful only if it can be restored within requirements.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 3}, {"id": "infrastructure-04", "category": "infrastructure", "category_name": "Servers & IT Infrastructure", "difficulty": "Intermediate", "type": "multiple-choice", "title": "A service is unavailable after a configuration change. What is useful", "prompt": "A service is unavailable after a configuration change. What is useful?", "options": ["Review change record and logs; consider approved rollback", "Delete all logs", "Disable firewall permanently", "Rebuild every server"], "explanation": "Correlate outage timing with the change and follow rollback procedure.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 4}, {"id": "infrastructure-05", "category": "infrastructure", "category_name": "Servers & IT Infrastructure", "difficulty": "Intermediate", "type": "scenario", "title": "What does monitoring help administrators detect", "prompt": "What does monitoring help administrators detect?", "options": ["Availability, resource pressure and service anomalies", "Keyboard wear only", "User favourite apps", "Desk temperature"], "explanation": "Monitoring helps identify service and infrastructure health issues.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 5}, {"id": "infrastructure-06", "category": "infrastructure", "category_name": "Servers & IT Infrastructure", "difficulty": "Intermediate", "type": "multiple-choice", "title": "A server certificate is expired. What should be done", "prompt": "A server certificate is expired. What should be done?", "options": ["Validate service identity and renew through approved certificate process", "Ignore browser warnings", "Disable TLS", "Share private key publicly"], "explanation": "Renew certificates securely and protect private keys.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 6}, {"id": "infrastructure-07", "category": "infrastructure", "category_name": "Servers & IT Infrastructure", "difficulty": "Advanced", "type": "scenario", "title": "Why separate administrator accounts from everyday accounts", "prompt": "Why separate administrator accounts from everyday accounts?", "options": ["Reduce exposure of privileged credentials", "Make email faster", "Increase screen resolution", "Avoid backups"], "explanation": "Use privileged access only when needed to limit impact of compromise.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 7}, {"id": "infrastructure-08", "category": "infrastructure", "category_name": "Servers & IT Infrastructure", "difficulty": "Advanced", "type": "identify-the-error", "title": "A backup job reports success but restore fails. What next", "prompt": "A backup job reports success but restore fails. What next?", "options": ["Investigate backup integrity and restore process; escalate incident", "Assume data is safe", "Delete remaining backups", "Disable alerts"], "explanation": "Treat failed restore as a serious recovery gap and investigate.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 8}, {"id": "infrastructure-09", "category": "infrastructure", "category_name": "Servers & IT Infrastructure", "difficulty": "Advanced", "type": "multiple-choice", "title": "A DNS record change is requested. What is important", "prompt": "A DNS record change is requested. What is important?", "options": ["Verify owner, target, approval and change window", "Change any record immediately", "Publish credentials in notes", "Disable DNS security"], "explanation": "DNS changes can affect services; validate and document them.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 9}, {"id": "infrastructure-10", "category": "infrastructure", "category_name": "Servers & IT Infrastructure", "difficulty": "Advanced", "type": "scenario", "title": "A critical server alert occurs outside business hours. What should happen", "prompt": "A critical server alert occurs outside business hours. What should happen?", "options": ["Follow the documented incident escalation and response plan", "Wait until someone notices", "Post admin password in chat", "Turn off monitoring"], "explanation": "Use the agreed on-call and incident escalation process.", "hint": "Start with the simplest safe check. Gather evidence before replacing components or changing settings.", "sort_order": 10}]$seed$::jsonb) as x(id text,category text,category_name text,difficulty text,type text,title text,prompt text,options jsonb,explanation text,hint text,sort_order integer)
on conflict (id) do update set category=excluded.category,category_name=excluded.category_name,difficulty=excluded.difficulty,type=excluded.type,title=excluded.title,prompt=excluded.prompt,options=excluded.options,explanation=excluded.explanation,hint=excluded.hint,sort_order=excluded.sort_order;


create table if not exists public.it_user_progress (user_id uuid primary key references auth.users(id) on delete cascade, xp integer not null default 0, level integer not null default 1, current_streak integer not null default 0, longest_streak integer not null default 0, last_activity_date date, completed_count integer not null default 0, updated_at timestamptz not null default now());
alter table public.it_user_progress enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "Users read own IT progress" on public.it_user_progress;
create policy "Users read own IT progress" on public.it_user_progress for select to authenticated using (auth.uid() = user_id);

create table if not exists public.it_challenge_attempts (id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), user_id uuid not null references auth.users(id) on delete cascade, challenge_id text not null references public.it_challenges(id), selected_answer integer not null, is_correct boolean not null, xp_awarded integer not null default 0, attempted_at timestamptz not null default now());
alter table public.it_challenge_attempts enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "Users read own IT attempts" on public.it_challenge_attempts;
create policy "Users read own IT attempts" on public.it_challenge_attempts for select to authenticated using (auth.uid() = user_id);

create table if not exists public.it_badges (id text primary key, name text not null, description text not null, icon text not null, threshold integer not null default 1);
insert into public.it_badges(id,name,description,icon,threshold) values ('first-fix','First Fix','Complete your first IT challenge','wrench',1),('challenge-10','Problem Solver','Complete 10 IT challenges','brain',10),('challenge-25','IT Explorer','Complete 25 IT challenges','compass',25),('challenge-50','IT Specialist','Complete 50 IT challenges','shield-check',50),('challenge-80','IT Master','Complete all 80 IT challenges','trophy',80),('streak-3','Three-day Streak','Learn on three consecutive days','flame',3),('streak-7','Week of Learning','Learn on seven consecutive days','calendar-check',7),('hardware-5','Hardware Foundations','Complete five hardware challenges','cpu',5),('operating-systems-5','System Explorer','Complete five operating-system challenges','monitor',5),('networking-5','Network Navigator','Complete five networking challenges','wifi',5),('cybersecurity-5','Cyber Aware','Complete five cybersecurity challenges','shield-check',5),('troubleshooting-5','Troubleshooting Thinker','Complete five troubleshooting challenges','wrench',5),('printers-5','Device Helper','Complete five printer and device challenges','printer',5),('cloud-5','Cloud Collaborator','Complete five cloud and productivity challenges','cloud',5),('infrastructure-5','Infrastructure Learner','Complete five infrastructure challenges','server',5) on conflict(id) do nothing;
alter table public.it_badges enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "IT badges readable" on public.it_badges;
create policy "IT badges readable" on public.it_badges for select using (true);

create table if not exists public.it_user_badges(user_id uuid not null references auth.users(id) on delete cascade,badge_id text not null references public.it_badges(id),earned_at timestamptz not null default now(),primary key(user_id,badge_id));
alter table public.it_user_badges enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "Users read own IT badges" on public.it_user_badges;
create policy "Users read own IT badges" on public.it_user_badges for select to authenticated using (auth.uid() = user_id);

create table if not exists public.it_daily_challenges(challenge_date date primary key,challenge_id text not null references public.it_challenges(id));
alter table public.it_daily_challenges enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "Daily challenges readable" on public.it_daily_challenges;
create policy "Daily challenges readable" on public.it_daily_challenges for select using (true);
insert into public.it_daily_challenges(challenge_date,challenge_id) select current_date + n, (array(select id from public.it_challenges order by id))[((n % 80)+1)] from generate_series(0,365) as gs(n) on conflict(challenge_date) do nothing;

create table if not exists public.it_daily_completions(user_id uuid not null references auth.users(id) on delete cascade,challenge_date date not null,challenge_id text not null references public.it_challenges(id),completed_at timestamptz not null default now(),primary key(user_id,challenge_date));
alter table public.it_daily_completions enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "Users read own daily completions" on public.it_daily_completions;
create policy "Users read own daily completions" on public.it_daily_completions for select to authenticated using (auth.uid()=user_id);

create table if not exists public.it_support_admins(user_id uuid primary key references auth.users(id) on delete cascade,created_at timestamptz not null default now());
alter table public.it_support_admins enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "Admins can read own admin grant" on public.it_support_admins;
create policy "Admins can read own admin grant" on public.it_support_admins for select to authenticated using (auth.uid() = user_id);

create table if not exists public.it_support_tickets(id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),ticket_number text unique not null default ('DESIQ-' || upper(substr(replace(gen_random_uuid()::text,'-',''),1,8))),user_id uuid not null references auth.users(id) on delete cascade,subject text not null,category text not null,device text not null,operating_system text not null,description text not null,attachment_path text,priority text not null default 'Normal' check(priority in ('Low','Normal','High','Critical')),status text not null default 'Submitted' check(status in ('Submitted','In Progress','Waiting for User','Resolved','Closed')),resolution text,created_at timestamptz not null default now(),updated_at timestamptz not null default now());
alter table public.it_support_tickets enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "Users read own tickets" on public.it_support_tickets;
create policy "Users read own tickets" on public.it_support_tickets for select to authenticated using (auth.uid() = user_id or exists(select 1 from public.it_support_admins a where a.user_id=auth.uid()));
drop policy if exists "Users create own tickets" on public.it_support_tickets;
create policy "Users create own tickets" on public.it_support_tickets for insert to authenticated with check (auth.uid() = user_id);
drop policy if exists "Admins update tickets" on public.it_support_tickets;
create policy "Admins update tickets" on public.it_support_tickets for update to authenticated using (exists(select 1 from public.it_support_admins a where a.user_id=auth.uid())) with check (exists(select 1 from public.it_support_admins a where a.user_id=auth.uid()));

create table if not exists public.it_ticket_messages(id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),ticket_id uuid not null references public.it_support_tickets(id) on delete cascade,sender_id uuid not null references auth.users(id),sender_role text not null check(sender_role in ('user','admin')),message text not null,internal_note boolean not null default false,created_at timestamptz not null default now());
alter table public.it_ticket_messages enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "Ticket participants read messages" on public.it_ticket_messages;
create policy "Ticket participants read messages" on public.it_ticket_messages for select to authenticated using (exists(select 1 from public.it_support_tickets t where t.id=ticket_id and (t.user_id=auth.uid() or exists(select 1 from public.it_support_admins a where a.user_id=auth.uid()))) and (not internal_note or exists(select 1 from public.it_support_admins a where a.user_id=auth.uid())));
drop policy if exists "Ticket participants insert messages" on public.it_ticket_messages;
create policy "Ticket participants insert messages" on public.it_ticket_messages for insert to authenticated with check (sender_id=auth.uid() and exists(select 1 from public.it_support_tickets t where t.id=ticket_id and (t.user_id=auth.uid() or exists(select 1 from public.it_support_admins a where a.user_id=auth.uid()))) and ((sender_role='user' and exists(select 1 from public.it_support_tickets t where t.id=ticket_id and t.user_id=auth.uid()) and internal_note=false) or (sender_role='admin' and exists(select 1 from public.it_support_admins a where a.user_id=auth.uid()))));

create or replace function public.submit_it_challenge(p_challenge_id text,p_selected_answer integer) returns jsonb language plpgsql security definer set search_path=public as $$
declare uid uuid:=auth.uid(); c public.it_challenges%rowtype; already boolean; ok boolean; award integer:=0; today date:=current_date; prev date; streak integer:=1; completed integer; totalxp integer; lvl integer; catcount integer;
begin if uid is null then raise exception 'Sign in required'; end if; select * into c from public.it_challenges where id=p_challenge_id and active=true; if not found then raise exception 'Challenge not found'; end if; if p_selected_answer<0 or p_selected_answer>=jsonb_array_length(c.options) then raise exception 'Invalid answer'; end if; select p_selected_answer=a.correct_answer into ok from public.it_challenge_answers a where a.challenge_id=p_challenge_id; select exists(select 1 from public.it_challenge_attempts where user_id=uid and challenge_id=p_challenge_id and is_correct) into already; if ok and not already then award:=case c.difficulty when 'Beginner' then 10 when 'Intermediate' then 15 else 20 end; end if; insert into public.it_challenge_attempts(user_id,challenge_id,selected_answer,is_correct,xp_awarded) values(uid,p_challenge_id,p_selected_answer,ok,award); if not ok then select xp,level,completed_count,current_streak into totalxp,lvl,completed,streak from public.it_user_progress where user_id=uid; return jsonb_build_object('correct',false,'xp_awarded',0,'xp',coalesce(totalxp,0),'level',coalesce(lvl,1),'completed_count',coalesce(completed,0),'streak',coalesce(streak,0),'explanation',c.explanation,'already_rewarded',already); end if; insert into public.it_daily_completions(user_id,challenge_date,challenge_id) select uid,today,p_challenge_id from public.it_daily_challenges where challenge_date=today and challenge_id=p_challenge_id on conflict do nothing; select last_activity_date into prev from public.it_user_progress where user_id=uid; if already and prev=today then select xp,level,completed_count,current_streak into totalxp,lvl,completed,streak from public.it_user_progress where user_id=uid; return jsonb_build_object('correct',true,'xp_awarded',0,'xp',coalesce(totalxp,0),'level',coalesce(lvl,1),'completed_count',coalesce(completed,0),'streak',coalesce(streak,0),'explanation',c.explanation,'already_rewarded',true); end if; if prev=today then select current_streak into streak from public.it_user_progress where user_id=uid; elsif prev=today-1 then select current_streak+1 into streak from public.it_user_progress where user_id=uid; else streak:=1; end if; insert into public.it_user_progress(user_id,xp,level,current_streak,longest_streak,last_activity_date,completed_count,updated_at) values(uid,award,1,streak,streak,today,case when ok and not already then 1 else 0 end,now()) on conflict(user_id) do update set xp=public.it_user_progress.xp+award,level=floor((public.it_user_progress.xp+award)/250.0)::int+1,current_streak=streak,longest_streak=greatest(public.it_user_progress.longest_streak,streak),last_activity_date=today,completed_count=public.it_user_progress.completed_count+case when ok and not already then 1 else 0 end,updated_at=now(); select xp,level,completed_count,current_streak into totalxp,lvl,completed,streak from public.it_user_progress where user_id=uid; if completed>=1 then insert into public.it_user_badges(user_id,badge_id) values(uid,'first-fix') on conflict do nothing; end if; if completed>=10 then insert into public.it_user_badges(user_id,badge_id) values(uid,'challenge-10') on conflict do nothing; end if; if completed>=25 then insert into public.it_user_badges(user_id,badge_id) values(uid,'challenge-25') on conflict do nothing; end if; if completed>=50 then insert into public.it_user_badges(user_id,badge_id) values(uid,'challenge-50') on conflict do nothing; end if; if completed>=80 then insert into public.it_user_badges(user_id,badge_id) values(uid,'challenge-80') on conflict do nothing; end if; if streak>=3 then insert into public.it_user_badges(user_id,badge_id) values(uid,'streak-3') on conflict do nothing; end if; if streak>=7 then insert into public.it_user_badges(user_id,badge_id) values(uid,'streak-7') on conflict do nothing; end if; select count(distinct a.challenge_id) into catcount from public.it_challenge_attempts a join public.it_challenges ch on ch.id=a.challenge_id where a.user_id=uid and a.is_correct and ch.category=c.category; if catcount>=5 then insert into public.it_user_badges(user_id,badge_id) values(uid,c.category||'-5') on conflict do nothing; end if; return jsonb_build_object('correct',ok,'xp_awarded',award,'xp',totalxp,'level',lvl,'completed_count',completed,'streak',streak,'explanation',c.explanation,'already_rewarded',already); end; $$;
revoke all on function public.submit_it_challenge(text,integer) from public; grant execute on function public.submit_it_challenge(text,integer) to authenticated;

create or replace function public.it_leaderboard() returns table(display_name text,xp integer,level integer,completed_count integer) language sql security definer set search_path=public as $$ select coalesce(nullif(u.raw_user_meta_data->>'full_name',''),'IT Learner'),sum(a.xp_awarded)::int,(floor(sum(a.xp_awarded)/250.0)+1)::int,count(distinct a.challenge_id) filter(where a.is_correct)::int from public.it_challenge_attempts a join auth.users u on u.id=a.user_id where a.attempted_at>=now()-interval '7 days' group by u.id,u.raw_user_meta_data order by sum(a.xp_awarded) desc,count(distinct a.challenge_id) filter(where a.is_correct) desc limit 20 $$;
grant execute on function public.it_leaderboard() to authenticated;

insert into storage.buckets(id,name,public,file_size_limit,allowed_mime_types) values('it-support-attachments','it-support-attachments',false,5242880,array['image/png','image/jpeg','image/webp','application/pdf']) on conflict(id) do nothing;
drop policy if exists "Ticket owner uploads attachment" on storage.objects;
create policy "Ticket owner uploads attachment" on storage.objects for insert to authenticated with check (bucket_id='it-support-attachments' and (storage.foldername(name))[1]=auth.uid()::text);
drop policy if exists "Ticket owner or admin reads attachment" on storage.objects;
create policy "Ticket owner or admin reads attachment" on storage.objects for select to authenticated using (bucket_id='it-support-attachments' and ((storage.foldername(name))[1]=auth.uid()::text or exists(select 1 from public.it_support_admins a where a.user_id=auth.uid())));
drop policy if exists "Ticket owner deletes own attachment" on storage.objects;
create policy "Ticket owner deletes own attachment" on storage.objects for delete to authenticated using (bucket_id='it-support-attachments' and (storage.foldername(name))[1]=auth.uid()::text);
